<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15949" root="رعى" body-key="r">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَعْوَى</span></b>  and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رُعْوَى</span>: see the next paragraph. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2- 
[Both seem to be also substs. from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَرْعَيْتُ عَلَيْهِ</span>;
and thus to be <i>syn. with</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَقْوَى</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بُقْوَى</span>; and in
like manner, ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رُعْيَا</span></b>  is probably syn. with <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بُقْيَا</span>:
the radical <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ى</span> being changed into <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">و</span> as it is in
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بقوى</span>.] You say, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَا لِى عَلَيْهِ رَعْوَى وَلَا بَقْوَى</span> [<i>I
have no mercy nor pity</i> to bestow <i>upon him</i>].
(JK in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بقى</span>. [See <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بُقْيَا</span>.]) See also 1 in art.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رعو</span> [from which <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَعْوَى</span> in this phrase may also
with reason be regarded as derivable].

